# A technical drawing: pale lines on blue.
#
# Edges first, which arrive as dark lines on white, then the levels move to
# throw away everything that is not a line — without it the paper is grey and
# the whole sheet turns muddy once it is tinted. The gradient map does the
# rest: what was white becomes the blue ground, what was black becomes chalk.

param threshold = 0.55
param ink = #0d3b6f
param line = #eef4fb

adjust black-and-white
filter find-edges
adjust levels black={threshold} white=0.92
adjust gradient-map from={ink} to={line}
